# DET-006 — Suspicious Remote Network Logon

**Status:** Validated 
**Detection ID:** DET-006 
**Detection Type:** Windows Authentication / Lateral Movement 
**Data Source:** Windows Security Event Log 
**SIEM:** Splunk Enterprise 
**Tuning Record:** TUNE-001

---

## Description

DET-006 identifies successful Windows network authentication originating from a non-local source.

The detection uses Windows Security Event ID 4624 with Logon Type 3 and excludes empty and loopback source addresses.

The detection is intended to provide analysts with visibility into remote network authentication that may warrant investigation for lateral movement or unauthorized remote access.

---

## Detection Logic

```spl
index=* EventCode=4624 LogonType=3
| where IpAddress!="-" AND IpAddress!="127.0.0.1" AND IpAddress!="::1"
| eval detection_id="DET-006"
| eval detection_name="Suspicious Remote Network Logon"
| eval mitre_tactic="Lateral Movement"
| eval mitre_technique="T1021"
| table _time host TargetUserName IpAddress WorkstationName LogonType detection_id detection_name mitre_tactic mitre_technique
| sort - _time
```

---

## Detection Conditions

An event must meet the following conditions:

```text
Event ID = 4624
AND
Logon Type = 3
AND
Source IP is present
AND
Source IP is not 127.0.0.1
AND
Source IP is not ::1
```

